Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 01:03:31 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 1/4] Rollback ordering: decide only from a snapshot read
 behind a quiescence barrier

rollback-decision (6fd7a929) returned LEGACY_REDEPLOY_SAFE from a zero-count snapshot and only then said
"stop any C2 instance": a C2 enrolment in between made the plan recommend 0.1.8 against an enrolled account.

- cutover.py rollback_decision: any fenced/CAS account -> FORWARD_ONLY; zero counts -> LEGACY_REDEPLOY_SAFE only
  when the same vm-state.v2.sh snapshot shows the barrier (start guard absent, indexd inactive, no process, no
  controller/tool session) and the owner attests C2 activation and retries are disabled; else UNKNOWN with the
  ordered barrier steps. It states what the snapshot establishes and what the parser cannot.
- primary/vm-state.v2.sh: the pinned vm-state.sh plus one read-only allowLiveStart line.
- CUTOVER.md: R1-R5 (disable C2, move ALLOW_LIVE_START aside, stop indexd with the reviewed controller, read,
  decide); T1 quiescence is stopped, retry-disabled, drained writers; equal counts are never proof of no writes.
- rehearsal/main_rollbackorder.py: r2 19/19 on two real v28 indexers - the original decision is SAFE on a running
  zero snapshot, C2 then enrols and 0.1.8 cannot write, the new procedure says FORWARD_ONLY; the never-enrolled
  rollback is SAFE only with the full barrier and attestation and then works. r1 (driver defects) kept as failed.
